  "id": "Compound::DB00232 - Gene::760",
  "verbalization": "Methyclothiazide, a thiazide diuretic, is consistently linked to calcium (Ca²⁺) through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Methyclothiazide, as part of the thiazide class, binds to calcium, with several related compounds—such as Hydrochlorothiazide and Hydroflumethiazide—also exhibiting this binding property. This relationship is further supported by the presence of a common ancestor in the thiazide family, which implies a shared mechanism of action. The recurring evidence points to a direct interaction between Methyclothiazide and Ca²⁺, likely through a common pharmacological pathway involving diuretic action. The integration of these paths highlights a consistent molecular interaction, suggesting that Methyclothiazide may influence calcium homeostasis through a mechanism that is not yet fully elucidated.",
